<title>JAPAN: Japan June green coffee imports rise 10 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June green coffee imports rise 10 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's green coffee imports during June totalled 32,058 tonnes, up 10 percent from the same month a year earlier, the Finance Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Imports of roasted coffee totalled 61 tonnes in June against 187 tonnes in the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of green coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		  June 97	   May 97	   June 96</p>
<p> Total	  32,058	    33,907	   29,121</p>
<p> Brazil	  6,781	     7,784	    4,156</p>
<p> Colombia	5,252	     4,789	    4,900</p>
<p> Indonesia     6,411	     6,407	    5,412</p>
<p> Honduras	1,681	     1,455	    2,084</p>
<p> Guatemala     1,587	     2,047	    2,630</p>
<p> Vietnam	 2,058	     1,957	    1,428</p>
<p> Mexico	  1,082	     1,674		978</p>
<p> Tanzania	  684	     1,201	    1,121</p>
<p> Ethiopia	1,485	     2,618	    2,148</p>
<p>Total green coffee imports in the first six months of 1997 were 182,808 tonnes against 153,481 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Roasted coffee imports (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     June 97	  May 97	   June 96</p>
<p> Total		61		 140	     187</p>
<p>Cumulative roasted coffee imports in the first six months of 1997 were 1,041 tonnes against 1,053 tonnes the year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
